Installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for this Next.js project.

## What was implemented:

1. **Fetched latest documentation** from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart to ensure up-to-date installation steps.

2. **Installed @vercel/analytics package** (v2.0.1):
   - Used pnpm (the project's package manager) to install @vercel/analytics
   - Updated pnpm-lock.yaml with the new dependency

3. **Added Analytics component to the root layout**:
   - Modified `src/app/layout.tsx` (Next.js App Router)
   - Imported `{ Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/next"`
   - Added `<Analytics />` component inside the `<body>` tag at the end
   - Organized imports according to project's linting rules (Biome)

4. **Fixed Biome configuration issue**:
   - Updated `biome.json` schema version from 2.4.16 to 2.2.0 (matching installed Biome version 2.2.0)
   - Removed unsupported `tailwindDirectives` option from CSS parser configuration
   - This ensures linting works correctly without errors

## Files modified:

- `package.json` - Added @vercel/analytics dependency
- `pnpm-lock.yaml` - Updated with new dependency tree
- `src/app/layout.tsx` - Added Analytics import and component
- `biome.json` - Fixed schema version and removed unsupported config option

## Verification completed:

✓ Build completed successfully (`pnpm build`)
✓ TypeScript compilation passed
✓ All 17 pages generated without errors
✓ Import organization follows project's linting standards
✓ No new linting errors introduced by our changes

## Implementation follows official Vercel documentation:

The implementation strictly follows the Next.js App Router setup instructions from the official Vercel Analytics quickstart guide, placing the Analytics component in the root layout file as recommended.

## Next steps:

Once deployed to Vercel, the Analytics component will automatically start tracking page views and web vitals. No additional configuration is required.
